# Code ownership for the Panoptes repository.
#
# Ownership is declared per path. GitHub matches the last rule that applies to a
# changed file and requests a review from that owner automatically when a pull
# request touches it. A rule here is a review requirement, not a permission grant.
#
# Panoptes is currently maintained by one person, so the catch-all below owns
# everything. The path-scoped rules are commented out until the owning function
# has a GitHub team to map onto; they record the intended ownership model so the
# split is visible before it is enforceable.

* @toomhorvath

# Platform surfaces
# /gateway/          # AI Platform - model gateway config, routing, quotas
# /telemetry/        # AI Platform - OpenTelemetry collectors, pipelines, dashboards
# /automation/       # AI Platform - operational tooling and scheduled jobs

# Control surfaces
# /iac/              # Security - Terraform modules and landing-zone definitions
# /policies/         # Security - OPA/Rego admission and usage policies
# /evidence/         # Security - control evidence collected for audit

# Governance and operations
# /docs/copilot/     # AI Platform - assistant rollout and usage guidance
# /docs/finops/      # FinOps - cost allocation, showback, budget guardrails
# /docs/vendors/     # FinOps - provider contracts, commitments, exit criteria
# /runbooks/         # Service Management - on-call procedures and incident response
